# The author's example (55c1abc), in a method: Model and Other both named Structures of the unit, `Model: Other` is
# Model's call with Other -- not the assignment of Other to Model, nor a declaration of Other.  Not built yet: refused
# where it stands.  (At the root the same line makes the unit read Other as a field it declares, l2_unit_declares, and
# `Other:` is refused first as an assignment -- as before the ticket; reported, not changed here.)
Model:
    size_t: value 1U
Other:
    size_t: value 2U
fn: g () int
    Model: Other
    return: 7
end: g
int: r 0
r: g()
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: r; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
